# Tailwind v4 — canonical class syntax

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4** with gym theme tokens in `src/app/globals.css`. Prefer **built-in utilities**
and v4 naming over arbitrary `[…]` values and deprecated v3 names.

Tailwind CSS IntelliSense flags non-canonical classes as **warnings** (`suggestCanonicalClasses`). CI and
`npm run test` enforce the same rules repo-wide via `src/lib/lint/tailwind-class-syntax.ts`.

## Theme CSS variables

Use the **parenthesis shorthand** — not arbitrary `[var(...)]` values.

| Avoid (non-canonical)                           | Use instead                             |
| ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `text-[var(--gym-muted)]`                       | `text-(--gym-muted)`                    |
| `border-[var(--gym-border)]/40`                 | `border-(--gym-border)/40`              |
| `focus:ring-[var(--gym-primary)]/30`            | `focus:ring-(--gym-primary)/30`         |
| `has-[:checked]:border-[var(--gym-primary)]/50` | `has-checked:border-(--gym-primary)/50` |

Applies to all utilities: `bg-`, `text-`, `border-`, `ring-`, `accent-`, `shadow-`, etc.

## Linear gradients (v4 rename)

| Avoid                    | Use instead       |
| ------------------------ | ----------------- |
| `bg-gradient-to-br`      | `bg-linear-to-br` |
| `bg-gradient-to-r`       | `bg-linear-to-r`  |
| `bg-gradient-to-b`       | `bg-linear-to-b`  |
| (any `bg-gradient-to-*`) | `bg-linear-to-*`  |

## Aspect ratios

When the ratio uses **whole numbers**, use the built-in fraction utility — not bracket syntax.

| Avoid              | Use instead      |
| ------------------ | ---------------- |
| `aspect-[4/3]`     | `aspect-4/3`     |
| `aspect-[16/9]`    | `aspect-video`   |
| `aspect-16/9`      | `aspect-video`   |
| `aspect-[430/932]` | `aspect-430/932` |

Keep arbitrary brackets for decimal ratios (e.g. `aspect-[1.91/1]`).

## Z-index and flex

| Avoid        | Use instead |
| ------------ | ----------- |
| `z-[100]`    | `z-100`     |
| `flex-[1]`   | `flex-1`    |
| `flex-[1.1]` | `flex-1.1`  |

Remove duplicate focus outline utilities — use `focus-visible:outline-2` only, not both `outline` and `outline-2`.

## Spacing scale (rem / px)

When a size maps to Tailwind’s spacing scale, use the scale token — not `[Nrem]` or `[Npx]`.

Scale: `1` = `0.25rem` = `4px`. Examples:

| Avoid           | Use instead |
| --------------- | ----------- |
| `min-w-[3rem]`  | `min-w-12`  |
| `min-w-[200px]` | `min-w-50`  |
| `min-w-[480px]` | `min-w-120` |
| `max-h-[320px]` | `max-h-80`  |

Applies to size utilities and corner radius: `rounded-[1.75rem]` → `rounded-7`, `rounded-b-[2rem]` → `rounded-b-8`.

## Viewport units

| Avoid          | Use instead  |
| -------------- | ------------ |
| `h-[80vh]`     | `h-80vh`     |
| `max-h-[90vh]` | `max-h-90vh` |

## Border width

| Avoid          | Use instead |
| -------------- | ----------- |
| `border-[3px]` | `border-3`  |

Keep arbitrary values for `min(…)` expressions and sizes that do not land on the scale (e.g. `rounded-[1.35rem]`,
`max-w-[430px]`).

## When editing components

- New class names: follow the tables above before reaching for `[…]`
- Shared UI primitives (`button.tsx`, `input.tsx`, `card.tsx`) set the pattern — match them
- After edits: Problems panel on touched files should be clear (reload window if IntelliSense cache is stale)
- Before finishing: `npm run test` (repo-wide Tailwind scan) and `npm run lint`

## IDE setup

`.vscode/settings.json`:

- `tailwindCSS.experimental.configFile` → `src/app/globals.css`
- `tailwindCSS.lint.suggestCanonicalClasses` → `warning` (do not silence in source)
- Exclude generated paths only: `.next/`, `node_modules/`
